Upstream: none found (gh search 2026-11-21; m4b/goblin#542 and PR #547 are other overflows in the Mach-O parser).

On 32-bit targets three usize computations in the ELF and PE parsers overflow on attacker-chosen
fields: offset + size of the PE debug data directory in DebugData::parse_with_opts_and_fixup
(size 0xffffffff), offset + 16 + bloom_size * 8 (or * 4) and the bucket and chain offsets in
gnu_hash_len (bloom size 0x20000000 in a 64-bit ELF, 0x40000000 in a 32-bit one), and
max_reloc_sym + 1 in Elf::parse (r_sym 0xffffffff in an Elf64_Rela). The patch saturates them, so
the existing bounds checks and preads reject the input. The tests in tests/elf.rs and tests/pe.rs
set these fields in existing test binaries; they panic without the patch on i686 in the default
test profile, which has overflow checks, and pass on x86_64 either way.

The panics need overflow checks (`-C debug-assertions` or `-C overflow-checks`). goblin's build.sh
does not pass --debug-assertions, which turns both on, so on wasm32 and in other 32-bit release
builds the sums wrap instead: the wrapped offsets reach only bounds-checked preads,
Symtab::parse_with_opts uses checked_mul, and a wrapped max_reloc_sym + 1 of 0 loses to cmp::max,
so no suite harness crashes. The patch is kept as an upstreamable fix for 32-bit builds with
overflow checks. max_chain - min_chain cannot underflow (gnu_hash_len returns early when
max_chain < min_chain); the saturating_sub there is defensive.

